# scripts/check-render-contract-gbuffer1.allowlist
#
# VK-GBUFFER1-CENSUS-1 -- INVENTORY of Vulkan fragment shaders that write color
# attachment 1 (GBuffer1) with a raw `vec4(...)` instead of an rc_* helper from
# shaders/include/render_contract.hglsl.
#
# This file is the audit record, not a permission slip. Every entry is a CLAIM
# that was verified at source; the reason lines say what was checked.
#
# WHY VK IS ALLOWLISTED AT ALL AND GL IS NOT
#   The GL half of Census 1 is ZERO-TOLERANCE and has no allowlist: every
#   shaders/*.frag attachment-1 write routes through an rc_* helper today, and
#   must keep doing so. Vulkan shaders can include the same helpers by relative
#   path (water_geom.frag does). Older ports inline the helper's literal value;
#   those remaining writes are frozen here so they cannot silently drift.
#   It already had. See the color_prop_tier1.frag entry below.
#
# WHAT AN ENTRY ACTUALLY BUYS YOU -- READ THIS BEFORE ADDING ONE
#   An entry exempts ONE EXACT WRITE EXPRESSION, not a file and not a shader.
#   The literal alpha constant is part of the key. Consequences:
#     * editing 0.25 -> 0.5 in an allowlisted write does NOT stay allowlisted;
#       the key stops matching and the write is reported as a fresh violation;
#     * adding a SECOND write to an already-listed file is NOT covered;
#     * renaming the output variable is not an escape -- the checker discovers
#       the attachment-1 output name from the shader's own
#       `layout(location = 1) out` declaration, so `o_normal` is censused exactly
#       like `oGBuffer1`.
#   It ratchets BOTH ways: an entry whose expression no longer appears anywhere in
#   the tree FAILS as stale, so deleting a write forces the reason to be retired
#   with it rather than rotting here as a false record of what the tree does.
#
# WHAT AN ENTRY STILL DOES NOT BUY YOU (the residual risk, stated)
#   The key pins the VALUE and the SITE. It does NOT prove the value is the RIGHT
#   one -- that is a human adjudication, recorded in the reason. If GL changes a
#   class constant, these entries keep passing while silently diverging. The GL
#   helpers are single-definition in render_contract.hglsl, so that is a small and
#   reviewable surface, but it is real and it is why each reason below names the
#   exact GL helper and file:line it was compared against.
#
# KEY FORMAT
#   <repo-relative-path>::<write expression, whitespace-squeezed, incl. the `;`>
#   Line numbers are deliberately NOT part of the key so ordinary edits above a
#   site do not churn this file.
#
# TO SEE THE CURRENT CENSUS (including what is NOT allowlisted)
#   sh scripts/check-render-contract-gbuffer1.sh --list-vk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LIVE WRITERS -- these reach the shared scene normal attachment for real.
# (Verified: the prop/mech/terrain islands set colorWriteMask to all four bits
#  on attachment 1 -- vulkan_color_prop_island.cpp:1220, vulkan_mech_island.cpp:846,
#  vulkan_terrain_island.cpp:1318.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# STATIC PROPS. Inlines BOTH static-prop classes from render_contract.hglsl:
#   rc_gbuffer1_screenShadowEligible_noSelfShadow()           -> a = 0.25   (:39-41)
#   rc_gbuffer1_screenShadowEligible_noSelfShadow_alphaTest() -> a = 0.1875 (:70-72)
# selected off the same alpha-test predicate the shader already uses for the GL
# 0.5 alpha-test discard. Mirrors GL static_prop.frag:657-661.
# THIS SITE IS WHY THE CENSUS WAS EXTENDED: it shipped a FLAT 0.25, misclassifying
# every VK-drawn tree/fence as a solid prop, and the census could not see it
# because Census 1 globbed only shaders/*.frag. Fixed in VK-GBUFFER1-CENSUS-1.
# Known, deliberate residual: GL selects per PACKET, the VK feed only carries a
# per-TYPE alpha class, so VK's alpha-test set is a superset at packet
# granularity. Inert for every consumer that exists -- both constants sit inside
# rc_isStaticPropNoSelfShadow (0.1, 0.5] and inside the shoreline water band
# (0.15, 0.35). Argued in full at the write site.
shaders/vulkan/color_prop_tier1.frag::oGBuffer1 = vec4(normalize(vNormalStuff) * 0.5 + 0.5, alphaTestClass ? 0.1875 : 0.25);

# MECHS. a = 0.0 == rc_gbuffer1_screenShadowEligible() (render_contract.hglsl:27-29).
# Matches the GL producer mech.frag:428 `rc_gbuffer1_screenShadowEligible(N_gbuf)`.
# Class is unconditional on both backends -- mechs have no second class -- so there
# is no per-fragment selection to get wrong here.
# VK-PARITY-MECH-1: N is now the shading normal Nshade (== GL N_gbuf with
# StandardLit off: the geometric normal, normal-mapped for imported mechs).
shaders/vulkan/mech_tier1.frag::oGBuffer1 = vec4(Nshade * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.0);

# TERRAIN, main pass. (0.5, 0.5, 1.0, 1.0) == rc_gbuffer1_shadowHandled_flatUp()
# (render_contract.hglsl:95-97). Matches the GL producer this island ports,
# terrain_lod_chunk.frag, whose every attachment-1 write is flatUp (:863-2608).
# Terrain handles its own shadow in-shader, hence a = 1.0 (> the 0.5
# rc_pixelHandlesOwnShadow threshold).
shaders/vulkan/terrain_tier1.frag::GBuffer1 = vec4(0.5, 0.5, 1.0, 1.0);

# TERRAIN, CSM debug early-outs (uT.csmDebugMode 1..8, eight sites collapsing to
# one key -- the expression is identical at every one). Same flatUp value as the
# main pass above, which is the correct behaviour for a debug view: the debug
# colour goes to attachment 0 and the normal target keeps a well-formed
# shadow-handled pixel instead of a stale or garbage one. GL's equivalent debug
# early-outs do the same (terrain_lod_chunk.frag:920 etc.).
shaders/vulkan/terrain_tier1.frag::GBuffer1 = vec4(0.5,0.5,1.0,1.0);

# TERRAIN OVERLAY / DECAL (VK-PARITY-OVERLAY-1). (0.5, 0.5, 1.0, 1.0) ==
# rc_gbuffer1_shadowHandled_flatUp() (render_contract.hglsl:122-124), exactly what the GL
# producers write at every attachment-1 site: terrain_overlay.frag (the "four sites" noted at
# render_contract.hglsl:121 + the main write) and decal.frag. Both handle their own shadow
# in-shader, hence a = 1.0 (shadow_screen skips them). The decal pipeline REPLACES MRT1
# (GL: SRC_ALPHA of this a=1 value == replace), the overlay pipeline is opaque.
shaders/vulkan/terrain_overlay_tier1.frag::GBuffer1 = vec4(0.5, 0.5, 1.0, 1.0);
shaders/vulkan/terrain_decal_tier1.frag::GBuffer1 = vec4(0.5, 0.5, 1.0, 1.0);

# TERRAIN SKIRT. The skirt pipeline's fragment SPIR-V is baked from terrain_tier1.frag
# itself (CMake MC2_VK_SHADER_SRC_ALIAS), so the main-pass keys above already cover it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STRUCTURALLY INERT WRITERS -- the write is masked off in hardware, so its value
# cannot reach the attachment at all. These are exempt for a stronger reason than
# "the constant looks right": the pipeline state makes the constant unreachable.
# Verify the mask, not the constant, if you ever revisit these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# VFX PARTICLES. vulkan_vfx_island.cpp:228 sets `cba[1].colorWriteMask = 0`, so
# attachment 1 is write-masked off for this pipeline. The declaration exists only
# because the shared scene renderpass has two colour attachments and the FS must
# declare both. vec4(0.0) is the inert placeholder; GL's VFX path writes nothing
# to the normal target either. RISK IF THE MASK CHANGES: an additive particle
# would last-write-wins a = 0.0 (the MECH class) over whatever is underneath,
# which would both break screen-shadow classification and -- because 0.0 is
# OUTSIDE the (0.15, 0.35) water band -- punch holes in shoreline foam. If you
# ever set that mask non-zero, this entry must be re-adjudicated, not carried.
shaders/vulkan/vfx_particle.frag::o_normal = vec4(0.0);

# VK-PARITY-F1 LEGACY SHAPE (ground vehicles etc.). Ports shaders/gos_tex_vertex.frag
# whose GL write is rc_gbuffer1_screenShadowEligible(vec3(0,0,1)) = vec4(0.5,0.5,1.0,0.0)
# (render_contract.hglsl:27-29, gos_tex_vertex.frag:`GBuffer1 = rc_gbuffer1_screenShadowEligible`).
# The SOLID pipeline writes it; the ALPHA/SHADOW/ADD pipelines set cba[1].colorWriteMask = 0
# (vulkan_legacy_shape_island.cpp) so blended passes never touch MRT1.
shaders/vulkan/legacy_shape_tier1.frag::oGBuffer1 = vec4(0.5, 0.5, 1.0, 0.0);

# NATIVE VEGETATION. Matches rc_gbuffer1_shadowHandled_flatUp() in
# shaders/include/render_contract.hglsl:122 and gos_vegetation_card.frag's
# GBuffer1 = rc_gbuffer1_shadowHandled_flatUp(): up normal, alpha 1.0.
# The vegetation pipeline alone enables all four attachment-1 write bits;
# billboard, tube and mesh pipelines keep attachment 1 masked off.
shaders/vulkan/vfx_particle.frag::o_normal = vec4(0.5,0.5,1.0,1.0);
